There exist absolute constants $\kappa\in(0,1/10)$ and $Q$ with the following property. Suppose that $q\ge Q$ is a prime power and every proper subfield of $\mathbb F_q$ has order at most $q^{1/3}$. If $P$ and $\mathcal L$ are sets of projective points and projective lines over $\mathbb F_q$ satisfying $$\label{eq:inc-theorem-sizes}
 |P|,|\mathcal L|\le q^{1+\kappa},$$ then $$\label{eq:inc-theorem-bound}
 I(P,\mathcal L)\le q^{3/2-\kappa}.$$

Let the sets below be finite subsets of an abelian group.*


1.  *If $Z$ is nonempty, then $$\label{eq:inc-triangle}
     |X-Y|\,|Z|\le |X-Z|\,|Z-Y|.$$*

2.  *If $Y$ is nonempty and $|X-Y|\le M|Y|$, then $X$ is contained in the union of at most $M$ translates of $Y-Y$.*


3.  *If $Y$ is nonempty and $|Y-Y|\le M|Y|$, then, for all nonnegative integers $u,v$, $$\label{eq:inc-multiple-sums}
     |uY-vY|\le M^{u+v}|Y|.$$

Let $F$ be a field, let $A,B\subseteq F^*$ be finite, and let $G\subseteq A\times B$. Define $$D=\{a-b:(a,b)\in G\},\qquad
 J=\{a/b:(a,b)\in G\}.$$ Suppose that, for real numbers $n>0$ and $V\ge2$, $$\label{eq:inc-graph-hypotheses}
 |A|,|B|,|D|,|J|\le Vn,
 \qquad |G|\ge n^2/V.$$ Then there is $S\subseteq A$ such that $$\label{eq:inc-extracted-size}
 \frac{3n}{8V^2}\le |S|\le Vn$$ and $$\label{eq:inc-extracted-expansion}
 |S-S|,|S/S|\le 2^{20}V^{22}n.$$ Here $S/S=\{a/a':a,a'\in S\}$.

Let $B$ be a nonempty finite subset of a field $F$, let $E\subseteq B$, and let $K\ge2$. Suppose that $$\label{eq:inc-scalar-hypotheses}
 |B-B|\le K|B|,
 \qquad |B-eB|\le 2K^3|B|\quad(e\in E).$$ Define $$\label{eq:inc-scalar-exponents}
 C_0=4,\qquad C_{m+1}=3C_m+5,
 \qquad\text{so that }C_m=\frac{13\cdot3^m-5}{2}.$$ If $\lambda\in F$ has an expression in $E$ using at most $m$ operations, then $\lambda B$ is contained in at most $K^{C_m}$ translates of $B-B$. In particular, $$\label{eq:inc-scalar-sum-bound}
 |E+\lambda E|\le |B+\lambda B|
 \le K^{C_m+3}|B|.$$ These bounds are uniform over all such expressions and all choices of their entries from $E$.

There is no sequence of prime powers $q\to\infty$, each satisfying the proper-subfield hypothesis of Theorem <a href="#thm:incidence" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="thm:incidence">3</a>, together with sets $S\subseteq\mathbb F_q^*$ and numbers $K\ge2$ such that $$\label{eq:inc-approximate-subfield-hypotheses}
 |S|=q^{1/2+o(1)},\qquad K=q^{o(1)},\qquad
 |S-S|,|S/S|\le K|S|.$$

For every sufficiently large prime $s\equiv2\pmod3$, there is a set $Y\subseteq\mathbb F_s^2$ with the following properties. For each $d\in\mathbb F_s^*$, there is an affine line $\ell_d$ of slope $d$, and $$Y=\mathbb F_s^2\setminus\bigcup_{d\in\mathbb F_s^*}\ell_d.$$ For each $d\in\mathbb F_s^*$, every line of slope $d$ other than $\ell_d$ contains at least five points of $Y$. The map $$f:\mathbb F_s^2\longrightarrow\mathbb F_s^2,
 \qquad f(x,y)=(x^3,y),$$ is a bijection, and every affine line contains at least $s/8$ points of $f(Y)$. Moreover, if $a$ affine lines and $b$ individual points cover $f(Y)$, and $$\label{con-weighted-budget}
 a+\frac b2\le s,$$ then $a=s$, $b=0$, and the lines form a full parallel class. Consequently every such mixed cover has weighted cost at least $s$, and no cover of $f(Y)$ by at most $s$ lines contains two nonparallel lines.

The pairing $M$ on $\mathcal P_{s-1,s-2}\times\mathcal P_{s-2,s-1}$ is nonsingular. Consequently, $$\label{eq:detector}
A\in\mathcal P_{s-2,s-2},\quad
M(A,B)=0\ \text{for every }B\in\mathcal P_{s-1,s-1}
\quad\Longrightarrow\quad A=0.$$

For every polynomial $H(x,u,y,v)$ of degree at most $n-2$ separately in each variable, $$\label{eq:test}
\sum_{i,p,k,q}
J([ip],[kq])w_iw_pw_kw_q H(t_i,t_p,t_k,t_q)=0.$$
